{
  "schema": "orca.head_envelope.v1",
  "id": "ratrig-vcore3",
  "name": "Rat Rig V-Core 3.1 with Rat Rig Toolhead V1.0 (official 2024 vc3 front/back/duct, Rapido UHF, SuperPINDA)",
  "provenance": "Rat Rig V-Core 3.1 with Rat Rig Toolhead V1.0 (official 2024 vc3 front/back/duct, Rapido UHF, SuperPINDA) Confidence: medium. Sources: https://www.printables.com/model/1386249 (full RR V-Core 3.1 toolhead assembly STEP: Rapido UHF, plate, vc3 front, 4010 hotend fan, vc3 shroud, SuperPINDA on vc3 probe mount); https://github.com/Rat-Rig/RatRig-PrintedParts/tree/main/Toolheads/Rat%20Rig%20V-Core%203.1 (PP000347 back, PP000348 duct STLs); https://www.printables.com/model/915644 (official VC4 back/duct co-registered, used to recover the STL export datum). Base geometry = 1386249 assembly (same frame/tip as ratrig-vcore4). Its own old back and community duct were removed and replaced by the official 2024 vc3 back/duct STLs. Placement of the official STLs: the VC4 duct and back STLs, ICP-matched to the official VC4 assembly, share an export datum (STL x = +/-33.88 centred on the nozzle; STL z=0 = duct/back mating plane at y 37.9; Z = -y_stl + ~24.7). The VC3 duct/back STLs have the identical datum features (x +/-33.88, top edge y_stl -3.8, mating plane z=0), so the VC4 transforms were applied to them. Result: vc3 duct outlet lips at z 4.59 (2.3 mm higher than VC4's because the vc3 duct is 2.3 mm shallower at the mating face), vc3 back at z 8.6. Lowest non-nozzle part: SuperPINDA at z 2.0 (x -29.4..-21.5, y -24.3..-16.4), as set in the community assembly; its height is user-adjustable (RatRig/Prusa practice ~1.5-2 mm). Hotend: Phaetus Rapido v1 UHF (RatOS default for V-Core 3 is the original Rapido; a shorter HF hotend would raise the tip toward the duct and is not supported by this duct geometry). Silicone sock estimated at z 3.2. Original V-Core 3 (EVA 3) toolhead was not modelled. Nozzle: land radius 0.49 mm, 53.4-degree cone to Z=1.50, then the nozzle parts as recorded. Gantry: X beam underside 62.50 mm above the tip, Y -31.0..96.0, every X. Converted by scripts/nonplanar_heads/open_heads.py from research/head-envelopes/ratrig-vcore3.json (2026-10-13). Nozzle-tip frame +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Body axial/lateral margins 0.3 mm. Not calibrated.",
